out an application workflow configured by a financial services firm; AI capabilities; and workflow intelligence components to manage data collection and automate tasks throughout the loan origination process. In addition, the company offers application programming interfaces, which integrate the capabilities of technology, data, and service providers into software platform, as well as support services, professional and consulting services. It serves banks, credit unions, fintechs, and other non-bank mortgage lenders. The company was incorporated in 2012 and is headquartered in Novato, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Nima  Ghamsari | Co-Founder, Chairman, CEO & Head of Blend | Age 39 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 419 people. Revenue per employee of $295K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue falling 15%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $69K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Blend Labs, Inc. is a micro-cap technology business with a $255M market cap on $124M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -19% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +16.6pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -36% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 52% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $81,000 of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 9.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 23% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 9.9% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 190% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.8960180826835065},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-7.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 24% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (92% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.083},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 294% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Fo